{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116418",
      "title": "Accessing Parent Route Data From Inside Nested Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 279,
      "videoOrder": 266,
      "sourceHash": "a78b438065d3deb187f6a45fca8e18c4262f9740837e01164d63c01a6bd50e0b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 2.76,
          "en": "So now as a next step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.76,
          "end": 4.68,
          "en": "it would be nice to actually load",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.68,
          "end": 8.67,
          "en": "and display the tasks that belong to a specific user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.67,
          "end": 12.24,
          "en": "And for that we need to go to the tasks.component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.24,
          "end": 14.82,
          "en": "because it's in there where I actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.82,
          "end": 17.79,
          "en": "want to output my list of tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.79,
          "end": 21.84,
          "en": "So here I need to fetch the tasks for a specific user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.84,
          "end": 23.4,
          "en": "because at the moment I just have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.4,
          "end": 26.49,
          "en": "this dummy fallback property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.49,
          "end": 28.533,
          "en": "which always holds an empty array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.46,
          "end": 34.46,
          "en": "So how can we load the tasks for a specific user?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.43,
          "end": 38.94,
          "en": "Well, keep in mind that the userId is dynamic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.94,
          "end": 41.58,
          "en": "and is part of the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.58,
          "end": 46.05,
          "en": "And child routes also have access to this information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 48.78,
          "en": "that's encoded in the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.78,
          "end": 51.09,
          "en": "Therefore, you can extract this data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.09,
          "end": 53.613,
          "en": "just as you could in the UserTasksComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.87,
          "end": 57.9,
          "en": "At least almost; I'll show you one limitation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.9,
          "end": 60.63,
          "en": "and a workaround in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.63,
          "end": 63.723,
          "en": "But in general, you can get hold of that user ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.8,
          "end": 67.83,
          "en": "And if we had access to that userId,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.83,
          "end": 70.86,
          "en": "we could of course use the tasks service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.86,
          "end": 74.95,
          "en": "and there this allTasks Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.93,
          "end": 79.83,
          "en": "to then find the tasks that belong to a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.83,
          "end": 81.87,
          "en": "with a certain id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.87,
          "end": 84.93,
          "en": "So therefore, back in a tasks component file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.93,
          "end": 87.78,
          "en": "it would, for example, be nice if we could get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.78,
          "end": 89.85,
          "en": "the userId as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.85,
          "end": 94.08,
          "en": "So as a required input, which will be a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.08,
          "end": 97.89,
          "en": "just as we did it in the user-tasks.component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.89,
          "end": 99.18299999999999,
          "en": "at least initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.5,
          "end": 102.39,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could also use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.39,
          "end": 104.22,
          "en": "this activated route approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.22,
          "end": 106.173,
          "en": "That would work here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.88,
          "end": 111.6,
          "en": "But of course using this input binding approach is a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.6,
          "end": 113.34,
          "en": "more convenient and shorter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.34,
          "end": 116.25,
          "en": "and that's why I will use it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.25,
          "end": 119.07,
          "en": "However, at the moment, it wouldn't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.07,
          "end": 122.52,
          "en": "If you go to the tasks.component template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.52,
          "end": 127.52,
          "en": "and you temporarily try to output that userId here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.28,
          "end": 131.79,
          "en": "by reading that Signal, if you would try to do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.79,
          "end": 133.95,
          "en": "you would see that nothing shows up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.95,
          "end": 135.453,
          "en": "It's not being output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.56,
          "end": 141,
          "en": "because by default child routes do not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141,
          "end": 145.413,
          "en": "receive those path parameters as input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.37,
          "end": 149.85,
          "en": "They can get access to them with help of the paramMap",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.85,
          "end": 152.88,
          "en": "through the activated route, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.88,
          "end": 154.71,
          "en": "That would work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.71,
          "end": 158.52,
          "en": "But this input binding does not work by default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.52,
          "end": 160.62,
          "en": "for child routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.62,
          "end": 165.21,
          "en": "So by default, a component can only get the path parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.21,
          "end": 169.413,
          "en": "that belong directly to its route through input binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.28,
          "end": 174,
          "en": "If as a child route you want to get the path parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174,
          "end": 178.82999999999998,
          "en": "of a parent route, you explicitly have to tell Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.82999999999998,
          "end": 181.86,
          "en": "about your intentions by going to the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.86,
          "end": 184.59,
          "en": "where you configured the router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.59,
          "end": 187.11,
          "en": "And then there you need to pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.11,
          "end": 191.79,
          "en": "an additional thing to provide router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.79,
          "end": 196.77,
          "en": "You need to pass the withRouteConfig function to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.77,
          "end": 199.29,
          "en": "and you must execute that function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.29,
          "end": 202.337,
          "en": "and it is being imported from @Angular Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 203.675,
          "end": 207.72,
          "en": "WithRouterConfig takes an object as an argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.72,
          "end": 211.383,
          "en": "which allows you to configure this router in greater detail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.34,
          "end": 215.88,
          "en": "Now here are various things you could configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.88,
          "end": 218.52,
          "en": "and most of them are a bit more advanced.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.52,
          "end": 220.8,
          "en": "But what I do want to configure here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.8,
          "end": 223.323,
          "en": "is the paramsInheritanceStrategy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.7,
          "end": 227.55,
          "en": "This setting should be set to always,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.55,
          "end": 229.56,
          "en": "and this will then ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 229.56,
          "end": 233.67000000000002,
          "en": "that those dynamic path parameter values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 233.67000000000002,
          "end": 236.403,
          "en": "are injected into child routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.17000000000002,
          "end": 243,
          "en": "So with this configuration set in the TasksComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 243,
          "end": 246.723,
          "en": "userid will be set by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 247.8,
          "end": 251.19,
          "en": "And as a result, if you again try outputting it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 251.19,
          "end": 252.573,
          "en": "here in this template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 253.71,
          "end": 256.77,
          "en": "you will now see that you userId here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 256.77,
          "end": 260.073,
          "en": "And it does change as you change users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 262.26,
          "end": 264.18,
          "en": "So that's how you can get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 264.18,
          "end": 267.15,
          "en": "to that kind of data in a child component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 267.15,
          "end": 270.993,
          "en": "And now we can use it to load the appropriate tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
